# Project Map: Safe Retained Legacy Collateral Retirement

Status: completed
Type: project-map
Updated: 2026-08-30
Program Roadmap: PRM-0033

## Purpose

Retire the original generated Markdown corpus that remained after schema-2 cutover without
deleting file-owned truth, breaking durable references, weakening recovery, or leaving SQLite
aliases that falsely describe removed files as live sources.

## Desired Outcome

The canonical maintainer no longer carries obsolete generated source files under `work/`.
SQLite remains the sole document authority, operator navigation uses disposable lifecycle views,
historical paths resolve deliberately, and a verified external archive plus current rollback
export can reconstruct every retired document.

## Completed Boundary

- Owner-approved manifest `459326469b84ba91` retired 259 aliases at managed revision 885.
- Exactly the 259 hash-bound generated legacy source files are absent.
- All 456 excluded `work/` files remained byte-identical during deletion.
- The current 326-document rollback export and 715-entry external source archive verified with
  zero mismatches; retain the archive through 2026-09-29.
- Full post-retirement validation passed, with no stale paths, work-state findings, roadmap
  findings, or bootstrap-closure findings.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Exact scope and link inventory | One deterministic manifest classifies delete, preserve, redirect, and unresolved paths | current clean audit |
| Managed retirement machinery | Dry-run and guarded apply retire aliases and files atomically or recoverably | frozen manifest contract |
| Recovery qualification | Current rollback export, archive verification, checkpoint rebuild, and disposable rehearsal prove recovery | retirement machinery |
| Canonical retirement | Exact approved deletion and link transition with full validation | owner destructive authorization |

## Constraints

- Delete only generated sources recorded by `document_conversion` and approved by the exact
  retirement manifest.
- Preserve imported owner material, code, tests, canonical product documentation, provider
  instructions, raw evidence, recovery truth, checkpoints, content objects, and required
  projections.
- Never use path patterns alone as deletion authority.
- Retire matching `document_path_alias` rows through managed revision-accounted state.
- Recheck source hashes, link disposition, archive integrity, current database revision, project
  identity, and rollback evidence immediately before deletion.
- Perform deletion only after a separate explicit owner authorization of the exact manifest.

## Non-Goals

- Purging unrelated `.tool-shed/` scratch, telemetry, backups, or temporary rebuild databases.
- Rewriting Git history or deleting the external retained-source archive during this outcome.
- Moving file-owned artifacts into SQLite merely to enlarge the deletion set.
- Publishing or deploying beyond what later implementation changes demonstrably require.

